&lt;p&gt;MEDFORD, Ore. &ndash; The suspect in the November 23 Medford Police Department officer-involved shooting has been released from the hospital and lodged in the Jackson County Jail. The suspect, Shane Wesley Smith, 30, of Medford, received treatment at a local hospital for injuries sustained during the incident and has since been cleared for confinement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Smith is charged with unlawful use of a weapon, menacing, interference with making a report, attempting to elude police, reckless driving, and driving under the influence of intoxicants (alcohol). The incident will be presented to the Jackson County Grand Jury.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Jackson County Sheriff&rsquo;s Office (JCSO) detectives are leading the investigation. Further information will be released by JCSO or the Jackson County District Attorney&rsquo;s Office following Grand Jury proceedings. This remains an active and ongoing investigation. No additional information is available at this time.&lt;/p&gt;

